# No environment variables are required to build or run the web app.
#
# PRODUCTION
#   The app is deployed at https://www.gadaviral.com/app/ and the WordPress API
#   lives on the same origin at https://www.gadaviral.com/wp-json/gadaviral/v1/
#   — api.ts uses a root-relative namespace on purpose, so production builds
#   cannot be redirected to another host by stray VITE_* env vars.
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT (`npm run dev`)
#   The Vite dev server proxies /wp-json to the STAGING WordPress API
#   (https://gadaviral.com/staging/wp-json/gadaviral/v1) — see vite.config.ts.
#   The UI on http://localhost:5173/app/ therefore talks to staging with no
#   extra configuration and no CORS.
#
# OPTIONAL OVERRIDE
#   To point the UI at a different API origin directly (bypassing the dev
#   proxy), copy this file to web/.env.local and uncomment:
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://gadaviral.com/staging/wp-json/gadaviral/v1
#
# NEVER put WordPress passwords, database credentials, SMTP passwords, private
# keys or OAuth secrets here — everything in VITE_* is public to the browser.
